    <statement><p>Evaluate the limit:</p>
<p><m>\lim\limits_{h \to 0} \frac {\sqrt {h + 8} - 8} {h}  =</m>  <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>If the limit doesn't exist enter <m>F</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>F</p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



<m>\lim\limits_{h \to 0} \frac {\sqrt {h + 8} - 8} {h}</m> doesn't exist, because the numerator approaches a non-zero value (specifically, <m>\sqrt{8}-8</m>), while the denominator approaches 0.



</solution>
